CHECK 1a — accessible submission mechanism / button semantics: PASS
  Button retains its visible+accessible name "Apply Changes", is now
  type="submit" inside a <form hx-post>, mirroring the sibling pattern the
  worker cited (web/templates/components/whatif/conversion-sweep.html:86-100,
  the per-row roth-conversion apply forms — <form hx-post> + hidden inputs +
  <button type="submit">). No change to tab order or keyboard reachability:
  the button was already focusable; wrapping it in a <form> and adding two
  `type="hidden"` inputs (non-focusable, excluded from the a11y tree) adds no
  new tab stops. Verified against a REAL render, not hand-built HTML: added a
  throwaway Go test in a `cp -a` copy at
  /tmp/.../scratchpad/a11y-z/repo (internal/handlers/whatif/zzz_a11y_dump_test.go,
  discarded, not committed) that calls handleWhatIfSync through the actual
  templates.New() + handler pipeline and dumps the byte-identical partial:
    <form hx-post="/whatif/sync/apply" hx-target="#whatif-results" hx-swap="innerHTML">
        <input type="hidden" name="expected_scenario" value="whatif.json">
        <input type="hidden" name="plan_hash" value="50ffef8e...">
        <button type="submit" class="...">Apply Changes</button>
    </form>
  Wrapped this real render in light and `class="dark"` pages loading the
  project's actual built web/static/css/tailwind.css and ran
  `npx @axe-core/cli` (wcag2a/2aa/21aa/22aa) against both:
    LIGHT: 1 violation — color-contrast on `.text-xs`
    DARK:  1 violation — color-contrast on `.text-xs`
  Both hits are the SAME element: the "(12-month average, excluding Health
  Insurance...)" span, `class="text-xs text-gray-400 dark:text-gray-500"`.
  `git show HEAD:web/templates/components/whatif/sync-preview.html` shows
  this exact line (with these exact classes) already present, byte-identical,
  on master, outside every changed hunk — PRE-EXISTING, not introduced or
