  No other axe hit in either theme; no new landmark/heading/table issue (this
  partial has no h1/table — unaffected either way); no motion; no color-only
  status signaling was touched.

CHECK 1b — hidden inputs are type="hidden", not visually-hidden-but-focusable: PASS
  Both new inputs use `type="hidden"` — excluded from the accessibility tree
  and the tab order by the platform, not a CSS visually-hidden trick that
  would remain keyboard-focusable. No focus trap introduced.

CHECK 1c — 409/error rendering perceivability: FAIL (ACCESSIBILITY.md #5;
  WCAG 2.2 3.3.1 Error Identification / 4.1.3 Status Messages)
  Traced (not executed — per the a11y-checker charter, execution is the
  tests lane's job) the real code path for the new guard branches added in
  this task's sync.go diff:
    internal/handlers/whatif/sync.go:401  renderError(..., http.StatusBadRequest)   // expected_scenario missing
    internal/handlers/whatif/sync.go:404  renderError(..., http.StatusBadRequest)   // plan_hash missing
    internal/handlers/whatif/sync.go:419  renderError(..., http.StatusConflict)     // active scenario changed
    internal/handlers/whatif/sync.go:437  renderError(..., http.StatusConflict)     // dashboard data changed since preview
  These four branches are NEW — pre-task, handleWhatIfSyncApply had no
  scenario/hash guard at all (it called plain `saveAndRecalc`, not
  `saveAndRecalcIfScenario`); the 409 conflict path did not exist as a
  reachable outcome of this handler before Z2.
  `renderError` (internal/handlers/whatif/handlers.go:680-693) writes the
  error body but sets no `HX-Retarget` header. Traced the client side, real
  code, no execution:
    - web/static/vendor/htmx.min.js ships htmx 2.0.4's default
      `responseHandling: [{code:"204",swap:false},{code:"[23]..",swap:true},
      {code:"[45]..",swap:false,error:true}]` — 4xx/5xx do NOT swap by
      default.
    - web/templates/layouts/base.html:205-214 only forces a swap on 4xx when
      `evt.detail.xhr.getResponseHeader('HX-Retarget')` is present.
    - base.html:224-226's `htmx:responseError` listener only
      `console.error`s — no toast/banner/live-region fallback exists
      anywhere in web/templates/layouts/base.html or web/static/js/*.js
      (checked, only web/static/js/whatif-poll.js references a *different*
      htmx error event by name in a comment).
  Net effect: on any of these four new branches (most plausibly the 409s —
  a second browser tab switching scenario, or dashboard data changing,
  between preview and apply are ordinary concurrent-use races, not edge
  cases), clicking "Apply Changes" produces a response body that is never
  inserted into the DOM at all. Nothing is shown to a sighted user and
  nothing is announced to assistive tech — worse than an unannounced error,
  it is a *dropped* one; the button visibly does nothing.
  This is a new-content replication, not a pass-through of an untouched
  pre-existing defect: the SAME package already has the correct convention
  for exactly this situation — `renderRetargetedError` (handlers.go:695-699,
  used throughout handlers_scenarios.go, handlers_healthcare.go, and
  handlers_income_expense.go for validation/conflict errors on
  #whatif-results-shaped forms) sets `HX-Retarget`/`HX-Reswap` so base.html's
  beforeSwap listener swaps the error in. The worker had a correctly-wired
  sibling to follow for these four new branches and used the other
  (non-perceivable) primitive instead. The pre-existing 500 branch in this
  same handler ("Failed to sync from dashboard...", unchanged by this diff)
  shares the same underlying flaw and is noted as an OBSERVATION for
  provenance, but the four new 400/409 branches are what this task added,
  and they are the ones a normal user will actually hit.

